  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 has a 5% maximum but no sales stop for models above it, with a 36-month transition for existing models and no numeric interim cap, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) from a market ban. S5 sets a mandatory recall above 8 per 100,000, which applies to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S4 delays built-in suppression to 36 months, favouring Halcyon's cost position. S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, which affects both companies' unreported incidents."
